mid·voyage is a notebook from the middle of the work.

Most portfolios show the polished result. I also want to document the constraints, wrong turns, and small decisions that made the result possible. That is where the reusable knowledge lives.

## Building in public, carefully

Building in public does not mean publishing every private detail or pretending every experiment succeeded. It means making the reasoning visible: what I tried, what failed, what changed, and what evidence supports the final claim.

This gives future clients more than a gallery. They can see how I scope problems, protect human judgment, and turn messy operations into systems someone can actually maintain.

## Why the name fits

There is no perfect point of arrival. Tools change, businesses change, and the person operating the system changes too. The work is always somewhere mid-voyage.

This blog is where I keep the map updated.
